# Implementation Plan: Modernizing Global Notifications

This plan outlines the transition from static, emoji-based Bootstrap alerts to a premium, "industry-standard" notification system using **SweetAlert2** and **Font Awesome**.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This change will replace the standard top-of-page alerts with modern "Toast" notifications (for successes like "Add to Cart") and "Modal" alerts (for critical errors), ensuring a seamless and non-intrusive user experience.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component Name] Global Templates

#### [MODIFY] [header.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/views/templates/header.php)
- **Dependency Update**: Inject **SweetAlert2** (JS/CSS) and **Font Awesome 6** into the `<head>` section.
- **Refactor Notifications**: 
    - Remove the existing static HTML alert blocks (`.alert-success`, `.alert-danger`).
    - Add a JavaScript block that detects CodeIgniter `flashdata` and triggers a SweetAlert2 notification accordingly.
    - **Success Notifications**: Display as a modern, auto-dismissing "Toast" in the top-right corner.
    - **Error Notifications**: Display as a more prominent modal with a professional icon.

## Open Questions

- **Toast Position**: Should notifications appear in the **Top-Right** (standard for desktop) or **Bottom-Center** (easier for mobile)? I recommend Top-Right for the premium desktop experience.
- **Auto-Dismiss Timer**: Is **3 seconds** sufficient for reading a "Item Added to Cart" message?

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Use the browser tool to trigger an "Add to Cart" action and verify the Toast appears without the old static icon.
- Trigger a "Login Failed" or "Restricted" event to verify the Error modal displays correctly.

### Manual Verification
- Testing responsiveness of the Toast on different screen widths.
